{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205528-muramasa-the-demon-blades-a-fan-ceremony","id":205528,"title":"Muramasa: The Demon Blades (A Fan Ceremony)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T19:48:34-07:00","id":205528,"title":"Muramasa: The Demon Blades (A Fan Ceremony)","content":"A friend asked for something like this, so I made a ceremony to create cursed swords. Out of Deathmasks.<br /> <br /> It was originally going to be a submission to OPP, but I decided to go with something else.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vindae.tumblr.com/post/92031724900/the-demon-blades\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr link</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/lwck03jlk7xiayp/Muramasa.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">PDF version</a><br /> <br /> Long ago in the <i>Muromachi</i> period of Japanese history there lived a swordsman named Sengo Muramasa. Second only to Soshu Masamune, his swords were of legendary quality, said to cleave any opponent in two. They were also claimed to be cursed, incapable of being drawn without drinking blood, even going so far as to cause bloodlust in whoever wielded one of his blades. They were said to go insane, slaughtering their kin or even turning the blade on themselves if it couldn\u2019t have it\u2019s bloodlust sated.<br /> One of the most famous legends of the Muramasa swords was the story of a man who out of curiosity placed both a Muramasa and Masamune blade down in the water of a stream. The Masamune was said to gently push aside any leaves that came near it, parting them neatly and without incident. The Muramasa on the other hand seemed to draw in leaves and fish alike, causing unnecessary slaughter. The swords\u2019 reputation was only increased when Tokugawa Ieyasu, who lost his grandfather, father, and son to the blades, decreed they were to be destroyed.<br /> Whether the legends of the swords are true or not isn\u2019t something that many Sin-eaters concern themselves with. As is often the case, they worry more about what works, as opposed to what\u2019s the \u201ctrue\u201d story. And using a powerful Ceremony, Sin-eaters can create these \u201cdemon blades\u201d themselves.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Forging the Demon Blade (Ceremony<span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trinigan FG\"><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">)</span></b></span></span><br /> Forging a Muramasa requires a Sin-eater to have a Craft skill of three with a relevant Specialty, and in addition to the normal materials to make a sword, a Deathmask must be merged with the ore, and the blade is quenched in the water of two of the Underworld\u2019s Rivers.<br /> <b> Performing the Ceremony:</b> Once the necessary ingredients are brought together, the Sin-eater undergoes a ritual trance and begins to hammer out the materials. Plasm is used to help break apart the Deathmask and merge it with the ore, and the water from the Rivers is used to quench the blade. With every hammer and trip to the furnace, the blade lets out painful shrieks and wails.<br /> Each roll of the ceremony requires the hefty cost of three plasm and a point of bashing damage, representing the smith pouring her blood into the forge. <br /> <b> Dice Pool: </b>Psyche + Stamina<br /> <b> Action: </b>Extended (target number of 10)<br /> <b> Time Increment:</b> Each roll represents one hour\u2019s work. A Sin-eater can never work on the sword in a single day more hours than her Composure.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <b> Dramatic Failure:</b> The demonic nature of the blade lashes out, the offended Deathmask dealing aggravated damage to the Sin-eater equal to her Psyche score. The failure keeps her from being able to work on the weapon until the damage heals, and in that time she suffers nightmares and fails to regain willpower. Plasm cannot be spent to bulwark this damage.<br /> <b> Failure: </b>The Sin-eater fails to make any progress bending the metal to her will. She injures herself, taking lethal damage and losing Plasm equal to her Psyche score. She can\u2019t return to the bladeworking until a full 24 hours have passed.<br /> <b> Success: </b>Forging the weapon goes as smoothly as possible. Once the successes are reached, and the blade is quenched in the water of two Rivers, a deadly weapon is created. The Muramasa appears to be a normal, if exceptional, weapon. To anyone who can see into Twilight, though, the blade burns with a hideous blue-green foxfire, subtle under most circumstances.<br /> <b> Exceptional Success:</b> Through hard work and strength, the character manages to ignore the screams of the materials as she works them. She gains a point of Willpower back as if she\u2019d fulfilled her Vice.<br /> <br /> Muramasa blades need not be katanas, simply bladed weapons. An ax or a spear works just as well. Instead of the normal statistics, one of the Demon Blades has two less Initiative penalty, and deals Aggravated damage, even to creatures in Twilight. Every time an enemy is slain with one of the blades, it gains a reserve of Plasm equal to the victim\u2019s Health or Corpus. It holds a max of ten plasm. It also retains the abilities it had as a Deathmask.<br /> <b>Bloodlust (Condition)</b><br /> You know nothing but fury and rage. You have an enemy, and you will kill them at any cost. One of you is going to die. Chances are it won\u2019t be you, but there\u2019s no guarantee. <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Whenever you go All Out or spend a dot of Willpower, add +1 on top of the normal benefits. You can\u2019t spend Willpower to increase your Defense and you can\u2019t Dodge for as long as the Tilt lasts. In addition, your blade must deal at least two health levels of damage for every turn that it\u2019s out. If you fail to quench it\u2019s thirst, roll Resolve + Composure at a penalty equal to the amount of blood needed to fill the blade. Failure means you deal lethal damage to yourself to sate it, while a Dramatic Failure necessitates the full Aggravated. Success allows you to deal bashing damage to yourself, putting it away with only a taste of your own blood. On an Exceptional Success you manage to force the blade back in it\u2019s case without incident.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> You had the gall to draw a cursed blade. Now it thirsts for blood and refuses to stay your hand.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> You sate the blade with your own blood of the blood of an enemy. The blade can and will drink from the corpus of a ghost or geist as readily as that of a living victim, but many strange creatures in the World of Darkness refuse to bleed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T14:23:15-07:00","id":269495,"title":"","content":"A like but no comments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T15:11:25-07:00","id":269524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205528-muramasa-the-demon-blades-a-fan-ceremony?p=269495#post269495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A like but no comments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shameless self bump, Aspel? :P<br /> On a serious note, I saw this back when you posted it, and I was all like &quot;Should I write him a comment telling him that I had had that exact same idea for my own Geist chrorinicle? Nah, that would seem like I'm trying to be all 'good idea, but I had it first!'. Better not.&quot;<br /> My idea was very simmiliar, although not the exact same. I had the blades as needing to be forged in a very specific Underworld lake, and I had a &quot;Lady of the Lake&quot; kind of figure, whom you had to barter with to gain acess to the waters. I didn't have the condition either.<br /> I had an idea, which was simply that these blades were able to permenently kill any immortal being, regardless of its mode of immortality. No Blood Bather comming back, no Vampiric Torpor, no Mummy whatever and perhaps most importantly, no Sin-Eater revival. In my own game, theres a small but potent Krewe of Sin-Eaters calling themselves The Ebon Fang, who have a deal with the afformentioned Lady of the Underworld-Lake, and who act as a religious sect of assassins.<br /> <br /> Might be I'll shamelessly steal the condition. I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T16:29:23-07:00","id":270476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205528-muramasa-the-demon-blades-a-fan-ceremony?p=269524#post269524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shameless self bump, Aspel? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Shame is for the lame. I got a message that someone liked it, but no comments. I like comments more than likes.<br /> <br /> Also, on the subject of &quot;permanently kill things&quot;, if you're interested in &quot;existing&quot; non-fan stuff, there's the &quot;Sword of Dracula&quot; in <i>Armory</i>. I don't particularly like it, though, because it... is awkward mechanically (which I feel could be the subtitle of all the base gameline books. &quot;<i>World of Darkness: Second Sight: Awkward Mechanically</i>&quot; and so on). It could have just said &quot;if you kill someone, the sword eats their soul&quot;, but instead it gives this long, meandering paragraph or two about how you need to drain them of their blood and then... if they're somehow not dead, they'll die and it'll eat their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T05:14:34-07:00","id":272154,"title":"","content":"Hm. Not bad. I didn't know the sword did that. That might be a neat thing too, that Draculas sword is one of these Underworld forged swords? The greatest of all undead had a blade forged in the realm of the dead from a vicious specter? Not a bad plot point.<br /> Having looked it over, yes. The mechanics for the blade seems abitrarily complex. I much rather prefer the &quot;If you were killed with this blade, you're dead&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Have you considered making the forging or use of the blade a Synergy breaking point? Its one thing to destroy a Geist in and of itself, but to forge its last remaining mark on the world into an instrument of death and carnage, is another entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T12:44:29-07:00","id":275683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/205528-muramasa-the-demon-blades-a-fan-ceremony?p=272154#post272154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I much rather prefer the &quot;If you were killed with this blade, you're dead&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/xXrWRyn.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">People die if they are killed</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you considered making the forging or use of the blade a Synergy breaking point? Its one thing to destroy a Geist in and of itself, but to forge its last remaining mark on the world into an instrument of death and carnage, is another entirely. </div> </div> </div>Not really. I'm trying to look at Synergy differently, and keep it from just being Underworld Morality and make it more in-line with Integrity. Plus, it's just a Deathmask. You're not even destroying it, just repurposing it. Although if you screw up... then you do break it, and probably should lose Synergy. Might make <i>that</i> the Dramatic Failure condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}